{"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "query": "Unit tests for an Arduino Uno module: RPG dice roller with potentiometer, movement detector and base-5 digits on a 16x2 LCD. Pins: pin 14 INPUT dice selector potentiometer A0 (not connected in the test setup: reads 0); pin 6 INPUT movement detector, a HIGH->LOW change rolls (not connected: reads LOW); pin 13 OUTPUT LED_BUILTIN, on while selecting/rolling; pin 12 OUTPUT LCD 16x2 RS (E 11, D4..D7 = 5, 4, 3, 2). Arduino API used: analogRead, delay, digitalRead, digitalWrite, map, millis, pinMode, random, randomSeed. Libraries: LiquidCrystal. Library API used: begin, createChar, setCursor, write. Simulated devices: none. Functions to test: void jdr_set_delay_scale(uint8_t percent), void jdr_reset_state(), void jdr_init(), void jdr_loop(), void selectDice(), void selectDiceWith(int selectorRawValue), void rollDice(), void rollDiceWith(int switchState, unsigned long now), void updateMurasakiClock(), void updateMurasakiClockAt(unsigned long now), void printMurasakiDigit(int value), void printMurasakiNumber(unsigned long value, int littleDigitCol, int row), void printDiceType(int col, int row), const char *jdr_lcd_line(uint8_t row).", "embedding": [-0.020355224609375, 0.002910614013671875, -0.017059326171875, -0.0305328369140625, -0.0295867919921875, 0.00978851318359375, -0.005580902099609375, -0.0015764236450195312, 0.029327392578125, -0.00861358642578125, 0.00897216796875, -0.0640869140625, -0.0085601806640625, 0.058380126953125, 0.05340576171875, -0.0179290771484375, -0.007534027099609375, 0.01180267333984375, -0.031951904296875, 0.04449462890625, 0.0609130859375, -0.01739501953125, 0.07391357421875, 0.0029125213623046875, 0.00925445556640625, -0.04766845703125, 0.04205322265625, 0.0036029815673828125, 0.0217132568359375, -0.04229736328125, 0.0123291015625, -0.03289794921875, 0.0008420944213867188, -0.0219268798828125, -0.055755615234375, -0.0204620361328125, 0.035247802734375, 0.0251617431640625, -0.027496337890625, -0.03231